<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="69484" href="schedule/2019/spring/MCB/529/69484.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2019" href="schedule/2019.xml">2019</calendarYear><term id="120191" href="schedule/2019/spring.xml">Spring 2019</term><subject id="MCB" href="schedule/2019/spring/MCB.xml">Molecular and Cell Biology</subject><course id="529" href="schedule/2019/spring/MCB/529.xml">Special Topics Cell Devel Biol</course></parents><sectionNumber>VD </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Virology Discussion</sectionTitle><sectionDateRange>Meets 14-Jan-19 - 08-Mar-19.</sectionDateRange><creditHours>1 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>This course will focus on discussing primary research articles about viruses. Each weekly meeting will involve the discussion of 1-2 articles. Specific topics included will be at the discretion of the instructor and the class and are expected to cover a wide-range of virus related topics including molecular virology, virus-host interactions, viral pathogenesis, viral immunology, viral evolution, and phage biology. Viruses of eukaryotic, bacterial, and archaeal hosts will be discussed.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Graduate - Urbana-Champaign.</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>A</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2019-01-14Z</startDate><endDate>2019-03-08Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="DIS">Discussion/Recitation</type><start>01:00 PM</start><end>02:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>M      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>136</roomNumber><meetingDateRange>Meets 14-Jan-19 - 08-Mar-19.</meetingDateRange><buildingName>Burrill Hall</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Brooke" firstName="C">Brooke, C</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>